    <h1>Exercise Name: Leg Press (Wide Stance / Frog Stance variant focusing on Adductors)</h1>

    <u><b><h4>Overview Exercise</h4></b></u>
    The exercise shown in this video is the Leg Press (Wide Stance / Frog Stance variant focusing on Adductors).
Here is a complete breakdown of the exercise shown in the video:

 Name: Leg Press (Wide Stance / Frog Stance variant focusing on Adductors)
 Target Muscles:  Primary: Inner Thighs / Adductors (Adductor Magnus, Longus, and Brevis)
 Secondary: Quadriceps, Glutes

Movement: A figure is shown executing controlled repetitions on a leg press machine with feet placed wider apart and toes angled outwards.</div></div>
<pre><h1>How to Perform (Step-by-Step Guide)</h1><u><b><h4>1. Setup</h4></b></u>
Sit on the leg press machine and firmly press your lower back and head against the seat backrest.
 Place your feet high and wide on the footplate (wider than shoulder-width).
 Angle your toes outwards at roughly 30° to 45°.

<u><b><h4>2. The Descent (Eccentric Phase)</h4></b></u>

 Disengage the safety latches while holding the handles at your sides.
 Inhale deeply as you slowly lower the sled towards your chest by bending your knees.
 Keep your knees aligned with the direction of your toes (do not let them cave inward).
 Lower until your knees form roughly a 90-degree angle.

<u><b><h4>3. The Press (Concentric Phase)</h4></b></u>

 Exhale as you drive through your feet to push the weight back up to the starting position.
 Important: Do not lock out your knees at the top; keep a slight bend to protect your joints and maintain tension on the muscles.



 <h1>Key Benefits</h1>

 <b>◉Inner Thigh Hypertrophy: </b> Directly targets and builds the adductor muscles, which adds thickness and sweep to your legs.
 <b>◉Enhanced Hip Stability: </b> Strong adductors improve overall hip stability and lower-body strength for squats and athletic movement.
 <b>◉Joint Safety: </b> Provides high muscle activation with lower shear stress on the spine compared to heavy free-weight sumo squats.



 <h1>Recommended Sets & Reps</h1>

| Goal | Sets | Reps | Rest Period |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Muscle Growth (Hypertrophy) | 3 – 4 | 10 – 12 | 60 – 90 seconds |
| Endurance / Tone | 3 – 4 | 12 – 15 | 45 – 60 seconds |
| Strength | 4 – 5 | 6 – 8 | 2 – 3 minutes |

> Pro Tip: Focus on a slow, controlled negative (2–3 seconds down) and explode up to maximize adductor engagement without overloading your knees.

